id: pm-rl-baseline
title: Gate recursive proposals with paired held-out baseline evidence
description: "Build on PR #94 with a bounded title-feature learner, held-out item confidence intervals against incumbent and constants, and at least three measured recursive proposal attempts on the same public corpus. Preserve contamination, approvals, resource accounting, resume and cancellation. Report refusals honestly."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T16:53:13.328Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T11:27:27.524Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T11:27:27.505Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T04:21:47.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Randomized paired evidence accepts exactly when every declared baseline lower bound strictly exceeds the unchanged effect threshold, with ties refused; A bounded cycle records promotions and refusals on tracker items and resumes each declared phase boundary without duplicate fits or charges; Balanced intake candidates must beat the incumbent, both constants and the frozen keyword heuristic with paired stratified lower effects above the unchanged threshold"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[41]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T16:53:34.594Z",codex-agent,"Pre-change diagnosis: PR #94 uses one logistic weight times a strictly positive log-title-length feature. Its greedy classifier is necessarily constant, so more samples, higher learning rate or more updates cannot make it useful. The held-out set has 36 closed and 5 other items, so always-closed scores 36/41=0.8780487805; the stochastic reward correctly penalizes uncertainty and cannot be substituted with greedy accuracy. Eight updates and 256 samples learn the majority slowly (0.5980 then 0.6810), but capacity is the primary defect. Holding every identical projected length in one partition is conservative yet prevents renamed-input leakage; retain this exact split. Proposed bounded intercept plus hashed title-word vector has no status/ID features and keeps all title-identical inputs together. Add deterministic paired bootstrap confidence intervals over held-out items against BOTH constant actions and the incumbent, in addition to existing sampled, exact-improvement and gap gates. Increase only explicit approved fit/sample allowances; retain every failed frontier and never relax the gate. Existing prefix/rsipower items cover broader chronological forecasting and transfer, distinct from this snapshot-recognition child."
  "2026-10-21T17:00:36.485Z",codex-agent,"Implementation in progress: bounded 64-column title-only features plus an intercept, unchanged source-action importance weighting, versioned vector checkpoint digests and full resume verification. Item-paired percentile bootstrap uses 8192 deterministic resamples, 41 held-out items rather than 40000 repeated rollouts, and Bonferroni-adjusted intervals for incumbent and both constant actions. Existing sampled confidence/effect, exact improvement and gap gates remain additional requirements. A preliminary numerical probe still trails the constant baseline; no win is claimed. Explicit sealed retry_rejected exploration will attempt three generations while keeping refused checkpoints out of collection and preserving all per-job reservations. Legacy scalar programmes keep their exact identities and stop semantics."
  "2026-10-21T17:11:46.623Z",codex-agent,"Three real external attempts on the same public pm-ops commit and original split are complete: n_train=105, n_held_out=41, baseline=36/41=0.8780487805. Held-out expected rewards and nominal 95% item-bootstrap CIs: g1 0.8713980699 [0.7743570291,0.9668509885], g2 0.8645003749 [0.7683455624,0.9579166612], g3 0.8534392510 [0.7593053408,0.9436312068]. All three are refused against the constant; zero promoted successors. Every collection used the unchanged seed policy; the derived learning rates were 1,0.5,0.25. The baseline still wins and no gate was weakened. Each job charged 256 optimizer updates exactly once; 3072 actions were collected. Resume verified all three, preserved checkpoint bytes, launched no new job, and status agreed. Source inventory bytes are unchanged. Execution used a PATH without Git and a plain controller tracker. Complete metrics, adjusted paired differences and full digests are in docs/baseline-frontier-evidence.json. Diagnostic log-loss fitting was worse (first score 0.7492), so it was not adopted."
  "2026-10-21T17:11:53.431Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof in isolated source copies: removing only the vector fit dispatch makes the three-promotion capacity regression fail (1 failed, exit 1); disabling only application of the item gate makes the improving-but-below-constant regression fail (1 failed, exit 1). Restoring both functions passes the two focused regressions (2/2, zero failures/skips). No production source was modified during the ongoing release gate."
  "2026-10-21T17:17:10.389Z",codex-agent,"Draft PR #95 is open against main and explicitly depends on #94. The first expanded local release attempt failed the new Git-free fixture at its unchanged 280-second child deadline under concurrent shared-host gates; that failed attempt is retained and is not passing evidence. The obsolete full run and linked snapshot run are superseded. The synthetic fixture now selects ten distinct input groups per partition and declares 512 evaluation episodes, retaining 95 percent confidence, the 0.01 effect threshold, three real jobs, all replay/budget assertions and the original deadlines. The real public experiment still uses 1024 actions and 40000 evaluation episodes. Cache each policy probability once per held-out item during action rollouts, preserving every action seed and numerical reward while removing repeated vector dot products. Final source gates and linked acceptance will rerun."
  "2026-10-21T17:19:12.110Z",codex-agent,"The operational acceptance dispatcher now has in-process and Git-free coverage. A synthetic entry coordinate did not exist, so the shared launcher correctly treated it as an import and skipped execution; the test then reported missing evidence. Use the actual existing script entry path in those tests. This corrects the fixture without changing launcher semantics or production promotion logic. Source proof tests pass 3/3 after probability caching; final expanded acceptance and full gates are rerunning."
  "2026-10-21T17:23:49.154Z",codex-agent,"Latest-source replay of the original real controller tracker passes after probability caching and strict parser validation: all three refused generations reproduce, status agrees, checkpoint bytes are unchanged and no new job launches. The receipt records source hashes specifically for this verified replay, rather than pretending they were captured when the fits launched. The behavioral frontier and all candidate checkpoint digests remain identical."
  "2026-10-21T17:29:21.271Z",codex-agent,"Refined verification keeps three real refusal generations in-process and uses a separate single-fit/replay acceptance with a Git-free PATH, avoiding duplicate three-job work in two test processes. The independently recorded real public run still contains three non-git generations and unchanged checkpoint/budget replay. Confidence, effect thresholds, source coverage and all deadlines are unchanged. Added real-controller negative cases require the existing gap and insufficient sampled-evidence refusals to stop even when item-refusal exploration is enabled; only verified item-gate refusals may continue. Malformed coefficient and feature payloads and a missing corpus are also covered."
  "2026-10-21T17:33:26.459Z",codex-agent,"The original gap and sampled-evidence stop regressions pass through real controllers and read-only status (1/1). Bootstrap/capacity/constant-refusal focused checks pass 3/3. Bootstrap replicates now use native Float64Array numeric sorting, preserving all 8192 resamples and the exact percentile order statistics while avoiding an instrumented JavaScript comparator on every comparison. Dispatcher negative tests cover each missing coordinate. The superseded two-process three-attempt fixture retained a shared-host timeout; it is not a passing final-head receipt. Final expanded gates use one Git-free fit/replay plus the separate three-attempt in-process acceptance, with original deadlines unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T17:38:18.561Z",codex-agent,"Pinned tracker-linked acceptance passes 10/10 at its recorded snapshot, zero failures/skips, in 534.957 seconds. The separately added original-stop regression passes 1/1; native-bootstrap focused checks pass 3/3. Final latest-source replay again passes all three real refused generations with byte-identical checkpoints and no launch. Full CI exposed a fixture dependency omission: the tiny Compose image copies an explicit module list and lacked the new item-evaluation module imported by bandit. Add that module to its COPY list; production and LM Dockerfiles already copy all root TypeScript sources. Existing real Compose lifecycle tests failed before this correction and will rerun. Superseded branch CI runs are canceled or failed, not passing evidence; final-head npm/Bun gates remain required."
  "2026-10-21T17:43:23.265Z",codex-agent,"Integrated the latest #94 review commit 56e2854 by a clean merge into this feature branch; no push to the parent branch. Its typed output preflight and symlink/race regressions are retained. The parent epic records are inherited from #94, not rewritten. Final source is frozen while the complete isolated-identity Bun gate, final-head CI variants and expanded tracker-linked acceptance run. Superseded local npm coverage runs and branch CI attempts remain failed/canceled evidence, not approvals."
  "2026-10-21T17:46:35.606Z",codex-agent,"Additional evaluator-only diagnosis: the training partition is 77 closed and 28 other (77/105=0.7333), versus 36/41=0.8780 closed in held-out. The fixed length-group split therefore shifts class frequency by about 14.47 percentage points. Each 1024-action batch still reuses only 105 unique training inputs. All three real greedy classifiers predict closed for every held-out item and tie the constant; stochastic rewards remain below it. This strengthens the recorded frontier diagnosis rather than changing the reward, split, baseline or gate. Aggregate counts are added to the evidence receipt."
  "2026-10-21T18:01:43.740Z",codex-agent,"Combined-source replay at 4f64e31 passes all three real generations with unchanged checkpoints and no new job. Packed consumer acceptance also passes with explicitly installed PM CLI 2026.10.21 and Node 26.12.0: initialization, package activation, corpus build, one actual external fit and resume in a non-git tracker with a PATH containing no Git. Its seal exactly matches the original public corpus; it refuses the candidate against the constant, charges eight updates once, and resume retains the same single settled job, generation and checkpoint. The repo SDK pin remains 2026.10.17 as required. Full details and package digest are recorded in docs/baseline-frontier-evidence.json."
  "2026-10-21T18:10:37.470Z",codex-agent,"Final combined-code head 4f64e31576b952b35e918561cdb9f67ac981eb26 passes complete CI: npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26/Bun 1.3.14, each 696/696 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Every variant measures 50 authored sources at statements/lines/branches/functions 100/100/100/100 and 343 documented declarations. Strict tracker health, identity, zero duplication, production audit, attestation, packaging, changelog and CodeQL pass. Receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39646147464 . Tracker-linked expanded acceptance passes 11/11, zero failures/skips, in 503.097 seconds; packed PM CLI 2026.10.21 Git-free acceptance and latest-source three-generation replay also pass. The redundant older local Bun 1.3.5 attempt is superseded by the complete pinned CI after its real Compose lifecycle group passed; it is not counted as a full passing gate. All earlier failed/canceled attempts remain recorded. The constant baseline still wins and all three real candidates remain refused. PR #95 remains unmerged and no release occurs. Remaining edits are documentation/tracker receipts only; release the claim while leaving this item in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-21T18:21:08.382Z",codex-agent,"Post-release boundary: strict local pm health reports merge_fence_drift:2; its history_drift check is OK, and this child item passes strict history verification. Complete fresh CI strict health passes in all three release variants. The owner no-git contract forbids merge-driver work, so clone configuration and existing tracker advisories remain unchanged; no history repair or re-anchoring is performed. This is separate from the measured 100 percent source coverage and the refused learner frontier. Standing tracker-advisory work remains with pm-rl-9uz4. The claim is released and this child stays in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T13:57:43.396Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up after PR #94 squash merge: inspect and update draft PR #95 against origin/main using the same merge-only approach as PR #97. Preserve vector training, item-paired gates, all measured baseline-refusal limitations and draft status. Regenerate CHANGELOG.md and ignored dist rather than hand-merging outputs; run full unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Prior behavioral revert proofs will be retained where feature behavior remains byte-identical. Do not claim that any measured real candidate beats the constant baseline or promote this draft to ready."
  "2026-10-22T14:08:49.505Z",codex-agent,"Merged main 2663828 into draft PR #95. Used the known shared #94 content at 56e2854 to resolve the add/add overlap while retaining the baseline vector learner and item-paired gates. Explicitly combined the feature-bearing corpus rows with main locale-independent ordering; retained current main publication guards, complete source snapshots, locale regression and all added corpus regressions. Combined corpus and baseline tests pass 25/25, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; build and test compilation pass. Existing baseline runtime functions and feature tests match the prior reviewed head, so their prior revert proofs remain applicable. The epic ownership conflict retains latest main unclaimed ownership and merged context. Ran the prescribed pm merge reconcile once: one receipt reconciled, zero entries rehashed or patch-repaired, no remaining drift. Independently verified all existing main epic and prior baseline history bytes remain exact prefixes; history is append-only. Regenerated changelog and ignored dist; run full unchanged npm/Bun gates on this merged candidate. The three historical real attempts still have zero promotions and do not beat the constant baseline; preserve draft status."
  "2026-10-22T14:28:43.694Z",codex-agent,"Merged-head CI run 39793575010 has completed the Node 26 npm and Bun 1.3.14 release commands: each reports 701/701 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, and 100/100/100/100 coverage across 50 authored sources. Bun package graph installation passes. Node 22 remains pending completion. The newly linked combined corpus/baseline command also passes 25/25 through pm test in an isolated snapshot. Existing behavioral revert proofs remain applicable because this update combines unchanged baseline behavior with already-tested main corpus fixes."
  "2026-10-22T14:32:02.691Z",codex-agent,"Main-update validation is complete at source merge 07e12fdc23ba249de2eab8d570db3d20af40ca54. CI run 39793575010 completed npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26 with Bun 1.3.14. Every completed log independently verifies 701/701 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, 50 authored sources and coverage 100/100/100/100 at unchanged thresholds. All three release steps, fresh strict tracker health and Bun package graph installation report success; 344 declarations, lint, duplication, audit, attestation, packaging and changelog checks pass. CodeQL passes. Local npm ci, generated changelog check, dist rebuild/check and linked corpus/baseline tests 25/25 also pass. No new runtime behavior was introduced by conflict resolution, so the prior vector-dispatch and item-gate behavioral revert proofs remain valid; earlier external evidence still has zero promoted successors. Draft status and dependency pins are preserved. The final receipt changes tracker evidence only, with unchanged source and tests. No PR merge, thread reply or resolution, or package release was performed."
  "2026-10-22T14:33:32.173Z",codex-agent,"Final prepared-environment strict health is ok:true with only the existing telemetry queue, stale-item and legacy provenance advisories. Restoring the unchanged tracked attributes after prepare reproduces the pre-existing merge_fence_drift:2 advisory owned by pm-rl-9uz4; no merge tooling or attribute policy was changed. CI strict health passes after its normal npm ci prepare step. Existing item and epic history prefixes remain intact, and added tracker records pass the local-path privacy check."
  "2026-10-25T00:00:09.154Z",codex-agent,"Owner acceptance pass for PR 95 then PR 98: preserve newer main evaluation/card/CAS behavior, deliver mandatory paired incumbent and baseline gates as infrastructure, add randomized gate equivalence and equality refusal, repeat the public corpus in a plain tracker, verify bounded cycle recovery/concurrency, and use unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates. Zero promotions remain a valid measured result. No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-25T00:07:02.467Z",codex-agent,"Main merge preserves the newer bounded JSON decoder, policy-card/evaluation-plan paths, native CAS and truthful peer outcomes. Added a verified-receipt field to resumed refusal inspections and settle their process lifecycle under the existing controller guard before deriving the next rejected proposal. Seven real plain-tracker boundary schedules pass, including active peer-controller attempts and concurrent comment insertion. The permitted single reconciliation returned ok:false/no_receipt_set_proves_snapshot for the inherited epic reconciliation event versus newer main history. Every original record is retained verbatim, no history repair or force was used, and CI readiness remains blocked pending owner resolution under pm-rl-9uz4. Local managed pm-github has an SDK host-version skew too; fresh CI installs no local extension."
  "2026-10-25T00:07:34.231Z",codex-agent,"Fresh public-corpus acceptance passes on a git-free PATH and plain controller tracker. Same public pm-ops commit, 300 unchanged source files, 105 training and 41 held-out items, 36 held-out closed. Constant reward 0.8780487805, candidate rewards 0.8713980699 / 0.8645003749 / 0.8534392510. Three refusals, zero promotions. Resume verifies all three with unchanged checkpoint bytes and no new jobs; 256 updates per fit, 3072 collection actions. Fresh receipt appended in docs/baseline-frontier-evidence.json. An earlier local rerun exposed an accidental status-path edit; typecheck caught it, it was removed, and this fresh rerun completed successfully."
  "2026-10-25T00:11:46.803Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs in an isolated source copy with unchanged pinned dependencies: replacing only the constant-baseline predicate with false makes the new random-vector property fail (0/1, exit 1). Removing only resumed-refusal process settlement makes train/evaluate/refusal-boundary schedules fail the terminal-job assertion (exit 1); source restored after each run. Restored targeted evidence: gate/capacity/constant tests 4/4, refused-cycle boundary tests 8/8, successful vector cycle boundary tests 5/5, plus pinned pm test execution 4/4. Successful cycles preserve a real peer promotion author and collect generation two with the promoted first checkpoint. npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run build and generated changelog check pass. CI 40145536972 completed at 7c0b00da05b46cdf55c176948992a6cc44c96002: all three variants fail strict health on the preserved epic history divergence, so npm/Bun release steps are skipped and execute zero tests. These are missing full-gate evidence, not passes. Keep PR 95 draft; full write-path interleaving/crash certification and full-gate counts remain unestablished at this head."
  "2026-10-25T00:28:53.768Z",codex-agent,"Final PR 95 property review broadens the same 96 seeded trials to arbitrary crossing vectors, noisy correlated effects, clear wins and ties. Two isolated behavioral removals now independently fail 0/1 (exit 1): replace the lower-bound decision predicates with point means, or disable the constant comparison. Restored focused command passes 4/4 directly and 4/4 through the pinned snapshot runner. Updated tests also pass unscoped npm run lint and npm run typecheck. Earlier 8/8 refusal and 5/5 successful-cycle boundary evidence is unchanged. Final pre-property CI 40145782245 failed health in all three variants, ran zero release tests, and passed CodeQL. No current full-gate or exhaustive write-path certification is claimed. Keep draft and release claim without closure."
  "2026-10-25T02:10:03.928Z",codex-agent,"Continuation under explicit owner instructions: restore divergent items to main and re-record branch intent with pinned pm commands. The epic is restored from main and enriched with this branch gate, measured null result, files/docs and targeted tests. Main has no baseline item, so this healthy branch-owned baseline chain is retained for the subsequent PR 98 merge. Do not repeat the completed experiments or behavioral reverts. Earlier failing CI runs were tracker-health failures; full unchanged npm/Bun gates remain required."
  "2026-10-25T02:11:26.863Z",codex-agent,"Restoring the epic to main and re-applying branch intent removes its chain mismatch. The old branch-only reconciliation artifact is now obsolete because the corresponding divergent branch event was replaced by the owner-authorized main-based reconstruction. Verified the artifact does not exist on main, removed only that artifact and its current linked-file entry, and left every main record untouched. No force, history-repair or re-anchor command is used."
  "2026-10-25T02:14:03.869Z",codex-agent,"PR 95 tracker health is now ok:true with failed_because empty using the normal pinned binary and existing settings. The unchanged main provenance-domain advisory is non-blocking. Reinstalled only the README-pinned project pm-github 2026.10.4 to avoid the newer global extension host skew; retained the original tracked managed-extension manifest and dependency pins. The epic stream is checked as a byte-identical prefix-extension of main. No executable source, test, numerical receipt or threshold changed, so completed experiments and revert proofs are reused. Regenerate the changelog, release this claim, push the health fix and run the complete CI release variants."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:16.312Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Objective redesign starts from PR 95 and incorporates the latest PR 94 head. First measure the frozen public corpus: class balance, constant predictions, class-conditional rewards and feature/target information. Preserve the original negative result. Select and seal a tracker-useful objective before running successor fits; retain paired bootstrap, contamination and resource gates, and require constant plus fixed heuristic comparisons. No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:18.368Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Data-first analysis at the frozen public pm-ops commit: 146 items; old title-length split train 105 (77 closed,28 other), held-out 41 (36 closed,5 other). Always-closed predicts closed for every item: closed-class reward 1, other-class reward 0; overall 0.8780487805. Always-other reverses these and earns 0.1219512195. Held-out mean title lengths are 79.8611 closed versus 79.8 other; train 82.5325 versus 89.5. Inputs contain length plus hashed words, no timing/lifecycle information; current edited titles and snapshot status cannot support a temporal forecast. Three original rewards 0.8713980699/0.8645003749/0.8534392510 remain honest refusals. All 146 histories expose a creation title and type. Creation-title split gives train 104 (68 Issue,36 other), held-out 42 (22 Issue,20 other). Training-only word counts show usable routing information: publish appears in 15 Issue vs 1 other; npm 10 vs 0; pm 9 vs 22; ops 4 vs 13. These are associations, not independent generalization evidence."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:20.257Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Predeclared new objective: creation-time Issue routing from the first create-event title; target is the first create-event type equals Issue. This is intake triage, not a future-closure claim. Use stochastic balanced accuracy: half the mean correct-action probability within each class. All constant/random-input-independent predictors score exactly 0.5. Keep all 146 examples, original length-group contamination split applied to original titles, 64 title-only columns, training-only balanced collection, three bounded external attempts, 8192 paired stratified item-bootstrap replicates and the original 0.01 effect requirement. Four comparisons (incumbent, both constants, fixed keyword heuristic) use Bonferroni family confidence 95 percent. The heuristic is frozen before new fitting: whole words bug/fix/fail*/error/regression/security/refus*/reject*/corrupt*/broken/crash*. Its diagnostic balanced accuracy is 0.5988562 train and 0.6545455 held-out; it was inspected during objective diagnosis, so validation is adaptive and no independent final-test claim is warranted. No threshold, split or heuristic tuning after fits. Both classes must satisfy minimum item counts; rejected checkpoints never collect. Preserve all legacy programme identities and negative evidence."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:23.034Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Three predeclared real external intake attempts completed on the frozen public corpus (104 training,42 held-out; held-out classes 20 other/22 Issue). Balanced accuracy with 95 percent stratified item-bootstrap intervals: g1 0.6080315976 [0.5184090204,0.6933652525]; g2 0.5915538072 [0.5245356249,0.6579211102]; g3 0.5667374267 [0.5221832763,0.6118104112]. Either constant scores exactly 0.5 [0.5,0.5]; frozen keyword router 0.6545454545 [0.5340909091,0.7727272727]. G1/G2 fail adjusted incumbent/constant effects; G3 clears their 0.01 lower-effect bound but fails the heuristic. Zero promotions; every collector remains the seed. All three actual jobs charged 256 steps once; resume verifies three generations, byte-identical checkpoints, no additional jobs, consistent status and unchanged 300-file source inventory. No objective, threshold, split, heuristic or resource bound was tuned after fitting. Targeted legacy checks pass 6/6; full npm/Bun CI is pending."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:26.200Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Behavioural revert proof in isolated source copies: restoring only the original unbalanced evaluate function makes the constant-policy balanced-score regression fail (1 failed, exit 1). Disabling only the mandatory heuristic refusal makes the balanced-bootstrap regression fail (1 failed, exit 1). Restoring only cyclic majority fitting in fitVectorBatch makes the balanced-fit regression fail (1 failed, exit 1). Restored functions pass all three focused regressions (3/3, zero failures/skips). Direct objective tests pass 7/7 including actual external fit/status/replay on a plain SDK tracker and separately with Git absent from PATH plus GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES. Creation-time corpus building is also exposed through the existing extension command; final linked tests and CI will include that integration."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:29.332Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Additional original-task feature diagnosis: the same frozen keyword flag occurs in 17/77 closed versus 9/28 other training titles, and 8/36 closed versus 2/5 other held-out titles. It is not a closed-status indicator; title semantics describe the work, while snapshot status reflects work completion. Public source visibility and MIT licence were verified independently. The new target instead uses the creator's intake type; the fixed heuristic is stronger than all measured new candidates. Typecheck, build, test-build, lint excluding retained ignored runtime snapshots, docstrings (50 sources,344 declarations), zero duplication and identity audit pass. Full release validation remains delegated to unchanged npm/Bun CI as requested."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:31.751Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Pinned tracker-linked objective suite passed 7/7 with zero failures/skips in snapshot workspace context and PM context none (179.215 seconds). The project disables automatic test-result tracking, so this comment retains the result without changing configuration. Original legacy-focused suite passed 6/6; behavioral revert proofs are recorded above. The final standalone suite also exercises the installed corpus command and malformed-bound refusal. The PR will target main and explicitly depend on both 94 and 95; parent heads are verified ancestors before push. Full npm/Bun release CI is pending; no local full gate or merge/release claim."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:34.130Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Complete source CI at 3b818e645e5e189fafa6d136b53a8d031ac3809c passes: npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26/Bun 1.3.14, each 707/707 with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. Independently downloaded all three completed logs: 50 authored sources, statements/lines/branches/functions 100/100/100/100,344 documented declarations. Strict fresh tracker health, unscoped lint, identity, zero duplication, production audit, attestation, packaging, changelog, Bun install and CodeQL pass. Run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/actions/runs/39689016234 . Latest standalone suite passes 7/7; linked suite 7/7; Node 26 combined focused suite 13/13. The actual public experiment replays on validated source with all three refused generations, unchanged checkpoints, status agreement and no new jobs. The constant shortcut is removed by construction, but no candidate beats the frozen heuristic; zero promotions and no gate weakening. PR 98 remains draft against main, after 94 and 95; draft review was skipped and is not approval. No new pm CLI/SDK defect was found. A final documentation/tracker receipt commit will retain identical executable source and run final-head CI. Releasing the claim; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification. No merge or release."
