  "2026-10-25T02:20:38.490Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): PR 98 fresh real-data acceptance passes on the same public MIT tracker commit, git-free PATH and plain controller tracker: 300 unchanged source files, 104 training (68 Issue / 36 other), 42 held-out (22 Issue / 20 other). Constants 0.5; fixed heuristic 0.6545454545; candidate balanced rewards 0.6080315976 / 0.5915538072 / 0.5667374267. Three refusals, zero promotions, 256 steps charged once per fit and 3072 actions. Resume preserves all checkpoint bytes and adds no jobs. Fresh receipt appended to docs/intake-objective-evidence.json. The gate/objective/decision receipt are infrastructure, and no predictive win is claimed."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:40.426Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): PR 98 current targeted checks pass: randomized stratified rule plus bootstrap/projection/seal/fitting 5/5, remaining objective real-process/no-git/replay 3/3, main corpus publication and English/Danish ordering 3/3; pinned pm test snapshot execution 5/5. Behavioral revert in an isolated copy: replace only the heuristic refusal predicate with false; the 96-case property fails 0/1 (exit 1). Restore the predicate: 5/5 focused checks pass. npm run typecheck, npm run lint and npm run build pass. Conflict resolution includes PR 95 source 7c0b00d and all of main 0025c8b while preserving every original epic/baseline/lintruntime history entry. Strict health remains false for inherited epic divergence and the combined baseline history, plus the pre-existing local managed-extension version skew. No history force/repair/re-anchor, dependency bump or gate relaxation. Current full CI and exhaustive write-path certification remain required before ready."
  "2026-10-25T02:20:42.291Z",codex-agent,"Re-recorded PR 98 branch context after the owner-authorized reconstruction (historical result): Final PR 98 property review includes arbitrary crossing vectors and noisy positive-mean effects whose paired lower bound fails, alongside clear wins and equality. Replacing only lower-bound decision predicates with point means fails 0/1 (exit 1); independently disabling the heuristic predicate fails 0/1. Restored focused command passes 5/5 directly and through the pinned snapshot runner, with unscoped npm run lint and npm run typecheck passing. Completed CI 40146037802 at 8105fcb850828fd8b2773ed2057540b19035e245 failed strict health in npm Node 22, npm Node 26 and Bun Node 26: every release command was skipped, zero release tests executed, no coverage percentage measured. All three logs independently show the preserved epic/baseline history divergences and pending reconciliation; CodeQL passed. No history was rewritten or force-reconciled. Both PRs stay draft; full write-path and release acceptance are unmet. Original history audits retain all 1820/2121 records from PR 95/main and all 1769/2164 records from the PR 98/PR 95 parents. No new pm CLI defect filed; existing normal-reconciliation proof and managed-extension host skew limitations are recorded."
  "2026-10-25T02:23:45.699Z",codex-agent,"PR 98 tracker reconstruction is complete: the inherited epic is a byte-identical main-prefix extension, and the baseline item (absent on main) is a byte-identical healthy PR 95-prefix extension with twelve objective-specific comments, three files, two docs, both complete test links and the balanced acceptance criterion re-recorded through pinned pm commands. Strict health is ok:true with only the unchanged main provenance advisory. The automatic merge stale clone-local receipt was preserved outside the active store after normal reconciliation explicitly wrote no audit history; no force or history-repair command was used. The pinned CLI refused an in-place test-metadata edit under the broad peer range, so the complete test link was re-added through its supported constructor instead; package pins are unchanged. Real-data and behavioral-revert results remain unchanged and were not rerun."
